WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
How do you catch the exact neurons active during one experience?

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.280
During that moment, a linked group of cells fires together, then fades back.

3
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.620
Watching them fire only gives correlation, the lowest rung of evidence.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.900
It shows those cells carry information, not whether they drive behaviour.

5
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:28.760
To move past correlation, activity-dependent genetic tagging labels cells as they

6
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.860
fire. During a chosen experience, a specific group of neurons becomes active

7
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:41.160
together. A driver switched on by the firing itself gives those active cells a

8
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.500
lasting genetic label.

9
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.720
Quiet neighbours stay untagged, so the active group stays marked after firing ends.

10
00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:54.843
That lasting genetic tag lets you switch those exact cells on or off later.

11
00:00:56.263 --> 00:00:59.903
Now you can climb above correlation to two direct interventions.

12
00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:05.663
Turning tagged cells back on tests sufficiency: are they enough to drive the

13
00:01:05.663 --> 00:01:11.103
behaviour? Turning them off while the animal remembers by itself tests necessity.

14
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:13.897
Test the necessity switch.

15
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:19.817
Suppose you tag cells active during learning, then turn them off while the animal

16
00:01:19.817 --> 00:01:20.917
remembers by itself.

17
00:01:22.517 --> 00:01:27.937
Recall fails. Does that prove the memory was erased, or only something narrower?

18
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.870
Impaired recall does not prove the memory was erased.

19
00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:41.710
It shows the animal uses those tagged cells at that moment.

20
00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:48.290
Sufficiency and necessity answer different questions, so neither intervention alone

21
00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.270
locates a memory. Every rung of the ladder needs its own controls.

22
00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.250
Networks also share cells across memories, and circuits reorganize over days.

23
00:02:00.433 --> 00:02:05.853
In gut-brain sensing, Tan and colleagues used the activity-dependent driver TRAP2.

24
00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:12.133
It tagged neurons of the caudal nucleus of the solitary tract that responded to

25
00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.233
sugar reaching the gut.

26
00:02:14.553 --> 00:02:19.833
In 6 animals, silencing their transmitter release abolished development of sugar

27
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:24.073
preference. Innate attraction to sugar or sweeteners stayed.

28
00:02:24.073 --> 00:02:30.193
That separated first-sip attraction from learning, leaving the intestinal cell type

29
00:02:30.193 --> 00:02:31.193
open.

30
00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.747
In the gut, the same trick solved a rarity problem.

31
00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:40.507
Enterochromaffin cells make more than 90 percent of the body's serotonin.

32
00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:45.627
Yet they are under 1 percent of intestinal epithelial cells.

33
00:02:47.227 --> 00:02:49.667
Finding so few cells had blocked single-cell work.

34
00:02:50.867 --> 00:02:55.707
In 2017, Bellono and colleagues genetically tagged them in cultured mouse

35
00:02:55.707 --> 00:02:58.727
mini-intestines, then checked native tissue.

36
00:02:59.817 --> 00:03:05.177
In memory circuits, learning strengthens links among cells active together, forming

37
00:03:05.177 --> 00:03:11.077
a linked group. On this model, a close enough cue pulls the rest of that group back

38
00:03:11.077 --> 00:03:17.137
on. That is one proposed way recall could work, not a definition of remembering.

39
00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:23.577
Engram experiments tag those active members to test sufficiency and necessity

40
00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:24.577
directly.

41
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.460
Activity fades in moments, and watching alone stops at correlation.

42
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.820
A lasting genetic tag preserves the exact cells active during an experience.

43
00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.520
Switching them on or off then tests what role they actually play.
